244p|n|An open wooden vessel formed with staves, bottom, and hoops; a kind of short cask, half barrel, or firkin, usually with but one head, -- used for various purposes. ; The amount which a tub contains, as a measure of quantity; as, a tub of butter; a tub of camphor, which is about 1 cwt., etc. ; Any structure shaped like a tub: as, a certain old form of pulpit; a short, broad boat, etc., -- often used jocosely or opprobriously. ; A sweating in a tub; a tub fast. ; A small cask; as, a tub of gin. ; A box or bucket in which coal or ore is sent up a shaft; -- so called by miners. ; To make use of a bathing tub; to lie or be in a bath; to bathe.	a:yjq,62,4;1jda,55,1;7md,41,3;1vhw,36,3~yjq,62,4;1vhw,36,3;7md,41,3;1jda,55,1	n:6jh,110,3;1jda,65,2;1wf6,60,1;1t1c,54,2;285t,52,3~285t,52,3;6jh,110,3;1jda,65,2;1t1c,54,2;1wf6,60,1
