24d8|n|The act or result of turning over; an upset; as, a bad turnover in a carriage. ; A semicircular pie or tart made by turning one half of a circular crust over the other, inclosing the fruit or other materials. ; An apprentice, in any trade, who is handed over from one master to another to complete his time.	a:1o2t,71,4;1yz0,71,1;pvn,67,5;1afo,61,3;f3j,44,3;e98,33,3;16xy,27,4;r4f,25,2;xvm,21,4;1cwn,18,2~pvn,67,5;16xy,27,4;1o2t,71,4;xvm,21,4;f3j,44,3;1afo,61,3;e98,33,3;1cwn,18,2;r4f,25,2;1yz0,71,1	v:1a51,31,3;ber,21,1;16xy,7,1~1a51,31,3;ber,21,1;16xy,7,1	n:1yz0,81,2;nwn,80,4;1xc2,66,6;1vce,63,4;1mb3,56,5;qul,54,6;ber,47,6;1qab,34,3;o9q,27,2~ber,47,6;1xc2,66,6;qul,54,6;1mb3,56,5;1vce,63,4;nwn,80,4;1qab,34,3;o9q,27,2;1yz0,81,2	N:1o59,41,7;22d8,24,4~1o59,41,7;22d8,24,4
